(4948717, 717010, 76335, '<td valign="top">I <i>knew</i> this was two kids! Excellent job anyway -- should have finished higher.<br/> <br/><b>EDIT:</b> Okay, I didn''t <i>know</i> it, but I did suspect it. It certainly made me think. I checked out your external website, and you have a real gift for photographing children. And it looks like you have a couple of ready and willing models available at a moment''s notice. I look forward to seeing more of your work. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-14 11:12:02.</i></td>', 'I knew this was two kids! Excellent job anyway -- should have finished higher. EDIT: Okay, I didn''t know it, but I did suspect it. It certainly made me think. I checked out your external website, and you have a real gift for photographing children. And it looks like you have a couple of ready and willing models available at a moment''s notice. I look forward to seeing more of your work. ', '2008-09-10 21:51:12.000000', '2008-09-14 12:12:02.000000', 0),
(4948721, 717375, 41337, '<td valign="top">Quite a profound image.</td>', 'Quite a profound image.', '2008-09-10 21:53:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4948751, 716347, 37719, '<td valign="top">busted comment...wonder why...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-11 21:48:09.</i></td>', 'busted comment...wonder why...', '2008-09-10 22:08:30.000000', '2008-09-11 22:48:09.000000', 0),
(4948976, 717677, 83313, '<td valign="top">My in-challenge comment on this entry was more about trying to understand the message your entry was attempting to convey, than about the quality of the shot itself. I gave it a 4, which is what I give to something I feel is a good effort with major issues. I felt the overexposure was incidental and was not used in an effective manner that enhanced the image. It appears to be a shot that was backlit and happened to fit the challenge. I think this was a difficult challenge to do for everyone that entered. Hope this feedback was more helpful to you than my first comment.<br/> <br/>Edited to add: BTW, The political statement had nothing at all to do with my vote.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-10 22:24:45.</i></td>', 'My in-challenge comment on this entry was more about trying to understand the message your entry was attempting to convey, than about the quality of the shot itself. I gave it a 4, which is what I give to something I feel is a good effort with major issues. I felt the overexposure was incidental and was not used in an effective manner that enhanced the image. It appears to be a shot that was backlit and happened to fit the challenge. I think this was a difficult challenge to do for everyone that entered. Hope this feedback was more helpful to you than my first comment. Edited to add: BTW, The political statement had nothing at all to do with my vote.', '2008-09-10 23:22:09.000000', '2008-09-10 23:24:45.000000', 0),
(4949150, 717677, 72096, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yospiff:</b></div><hr/><i> My in-challenge comment on this entry was more about trying to understand the message your entry was attempting to convey, than about the quality of the shot itself. I gave it a 4, which is what I give to something I feel is a good effort with major issues. I felt the overexposure was incidental and was not used in an effective manner that enhanced the image. It appears to be a shot that was backlit and happened to fit the challenge. I think this was a difficult challenge to do for everyone that entered. Hope this feedback was more helpful to you than my first comment.<br/> <br/>Edited to add: BTW, The political statement had nothing at all to do with my vote. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thankyou, but I have no problem with a low score.  The title may have provoked political anger, leading to a poor opinion on the subject.  That''s fine.  I will know better next time.  BUT... I did not appreciate comments which had nothing to do with the technical aspects of the shot.  If you don''t like the subject, keep your negative comments to yourself.  Political comments have no place in this arena.</td>', 'Originally posted by yospiff: My in-challenge comment on this entry was more about trying to understand the message your entry was attempting to convey, than about the quality of the shot itself. I gave it a 4, which is what I give to something I feel is a good effort with major issues. I felt the overexposure was incidental and was not used in an effective manner that enhanced the image. It appears to be a shot that was backlit and happened to fit the challenge. I think this was a difficult challenge to do for everyone that entered. Hope this feedback was more helpful to you than my first comment. Edited to add: BTW, The political statement had nothing at all to do with my vote.   Thankyou, but I have no problem with a low score.  The title may have provoked political anger, leading to a poor opinion on the subject.  That''s fine.  I will know better next time.  BUT... I did not appreciate comments which had nothing to do with the technical aspects of the shot.  If you don''t like the subject, keep your negative comments to yourself.  Political comments have no place in this arena.', '2008-09-11 00:29:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4949170, 717677, 86090, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to vote on this challenge, I did look at the pictures though, and yours called my attention, at first because of the title (nothing wrong with it), I think the technicals you already mention them, lens flare and color saturation. Overall imo you did a goo job.</td>', 'I didn''t get to vote on this challenge, I did look at the pictures though, and yours called my attention, at first because of the title (nothing wrong with it), I think the technicals you already mention them, lens flare and color saturation. Overall imo you did a goo job.', '2008-09-11 00:41:48.000000', NULL, 0),
