(4949419, 717565, 39430, '<td valign="top">Yet another great image of your kids.  :)  You are right, she works so well for high key.  I love your composition here too.  Great work.  I always love reading about the shot too, so thanks for putting the time into your "Photographer''s Comments".</td>', 'Yet another great image of your kids.  :)  You are right, she works so well for high key.  I love your composition here too.  Great work.  I always love reading about the shot too, so thanks for putting the time into your "Photographer''s Comments".', '2008-09-11 02:30:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4949450, 717653, 47791, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NikonJeb:</b></div><hr/><i> Really nice entry! Well executed.....I''d love to know how you did this after the challenge. 9 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NikonJeb:</b></div><hr/><i> Really nice entry! Well executed.....I''d love to know how you did this after the challenge. 9 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I took a picture of my sister, her husband and their baby in the garden while it was sunny. <br/>I told them hold dead still and they did. Simple as that.<br/> <br/>Afterwards I simply cropped on her face as she had a cool expression. <br/> <br/><a href="//i3.photobucket.com/albums/y79/Liamsphotos/Sept%2008/OverExposed.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Original photo</a> <br/> <br/><a href="//i3.photobucket.com/albums/y79/Liamsphotos/Sept%2008/IMG_5442.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">UN exposed version. </a></td>', 'Originally posted by NikonJeb: Really nice entry! Well executed.....I''d love to know how you did this after the challenge. 9   Originally posted by NikonJeb: Really nice entry! Well executed.....I''d love to know how you did this after the challenge. 9   I took a picture of my sister, her husband and their baby in the garden while it was sunny. I told them hold dead still and they did. Simple as that. Afterwards I simply cropped on her face as she had a cool expression.  Original photo  UN exposed version. ', '2008-09-11 02:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4949666, 716347, 62357, '<td valign="top">Wow Andi, Well done!!!  Awesome</td>', 'Wow Andi, Well done!!!  Awesome', '2008-09-11 06:03:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4949823, 715429, 57882, '<td valign="top">I love the silky feel of this shot.</td>', 'I love the silky feel of this shot.', '2008-09-11 08:22:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4949830, 716347, 57882, '<td valign="top">Well done.  Nice control of the shadows.</td>', 'Well done.  Nice control of the shadows.', '2008-09-11 08:30:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4949875, 717677, 51793, '<td valign="top">I just read your post in the forums and thought I would check this picture out. Let me be the one to give you some information. <br/> <br/>I do see that the exposure is a bit off which does meet the challenge but there is more than that here. When people on DPC look at shots like this they tend to take offense to them. Politics are definitely a category that you and everyone else should stay away from just because people take crap way to seriously. If I had voted on this image I would have given it a 4 or 5. NOT because of your title or the fact that you would like your joke about your child being the next (or first) black president. <br/> <br/>I would have voted on the actual content and subject matter of your photo. <br/> <br/>So with that said let me tell you what "I" see wrong with it. <br/>Color range... the colors seem to be a bit faded. Because of the light bouncing back into the camera it''s fading all your colors which you could have saturated them in PP. <br/> <br/>Content... Although you kept the subject and BG simple there are some issues with it. The BG is crooked and your subject doesn''t even look like he is going to give a speech or even address anyone. It looks like you had the idea in your head of what you wanted the image to look like and so you set up the flag but when it got to the camera it came out different... Don''t worry a lot of people have that problem, me being one of them.<br/> <br/>Subject pose... Had you had a microphone or something in his hand it might have conveyed more of the Obama type of setting to me. Also having the subject turn more towards the camera some and then also look into the camera like he was serious about running, then if might have looked more realistic. <br/> <br/>Remember this about roll playing photography shots... You have to get serious about the character if you are going to play them. Even if it is a child... Have them watch clips of the character and you have to play with them to get them into the mood. Take my <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=682918" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">got milk</a> shot for example...  It took me 2 hours and over 120 shots to get that 1 photo. Yeah I got some others to but this is the EXACT shot I had pictured in my head. We watched youtube for 20 minutes, and looked at other pictures, I even had to let him shoot me doing the same thing just to get him into the character. <br/>I guess all I''m really saying here is if your going to do it... DO IT RIGHT.</td>', 'I just read your post in the forums and thought I would check this picture out. Let me be the one to give you some information.  I do see that the exposure is a bit off which does meet the challenge but there is more than that here. When people on DPC look at shots like this they tend to take offense to them. Politics are definitely a category that you and everyone else should stay away from just because people take crap way to seriously. If I had voted on this image I would have given it a 4 or 5. NOT because of your title or the fact that you would like your joke about your child being the next (or first) black president.  I would have voted on the actual content and subject matter of your photo.  So with that said let me tell you what "I" see wrong with it. Color range... the colors seem to be a bit faded. Because of the light bouncing back into the camera it''s fading all your colors which you could have saturated them in PP.  Content... Although you kept the subject and BG simple there are some issues with it. The BG is crooked and your subject doesn''t even look like he is going to give a speech or even address anyone. It looks like you had the idea in your head of what you wanted the image to look like and so you set up the flag but when it got to the camera it came out different... Don''t worry a lot of people have that problem, me being one of them. Subject pose... Had you had a microphone or something in his hand it might have conveyed more of the Obama type of setting to me. Also having the subject turn more towards the camera some and then also look into the camera like he was serious about running, then if might have looked more realistic.  Remember this about roll playing photography shots... You have to get serious about the character if you are going to play them. Even if it is a child... Have them watch clips of the character and you have to play with them to get them into the mood. Take my got milk shot for example...  It took me 2 hours and over 120 shots to get that 1 photo. Yeah I got some others to but this is the EXACT shot I had pictured in my head. We watched youtube for 20 minutes, and looked at other pictures, I even had to let him shoot me doing the same thing just to get him into the character. I guess all I''m really saying here is if your going to do it... DO IT RIGHT.', '2008-09-11 09:04:19.000000', NULL, 0),
