(4956676, 717242, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>I wanted to say that the photo was overexposed, but now I see that''s the challenge-topic ;)<br/> <br/>The first two things that I see here are the bright yellow colors and the natural framing. I like it!<br/>The darker contrast-rich rocks are great with the bright and soft view at the center. I think you did a good job. <br/> <br/>Bigger is better, too bad the resolution couldn''t be bigger.</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  I wanted to say that the photo was overexposed, but now I see that''s the challenge-topic ;) The first two things that I see here are the bright yellow colors and the natural framing. I like it!The darker contrast-rich rocks are great with the bright and soft view at the center. I think you did a good job.  Bigger is better, too bad the resolution couldn''t be bigger.', '2008-09-15 16:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956691, 717566, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>First of all, the composition is good. The statue is good in the frame and the (small) negative space on the left is well done.<br/> <br/>Having the challenge-topic in mind, I''m not sure if this fits. Ok, the subject is overexposed, but while overexposing one subject with backlight, the contrast goes way down and that way the photo is "just" overexposed. Try being creative with the technique is my advice.<br/> <br/>I hope this comment was helpful!</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  First of all, the composition is good. The statue is good in the frame and the (small) negative space on the left is well done. Having the challenge-topic in mind, I''m not sure if this fits. Ok, the subject is overexposed, but while overexposing one subject with backlight, the contrast goes way down and that way the photo is "just" overexposed. Try being creative with the technique is my advice. I hope this comment was helpful!', '2008-09-15 16:41:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956703, 716642, 42013, '<td valign="top">Wow, surprised to see this one finished squarely on 5. I didn''t vote in the challenge but this one caught my eye. As some commentators mentioned, the inclusion of the blue sweatshirt probably hurt you in the score department. It would probably have been less of an issue if Riley''s eyes were blue. I love the tilt in his head and the expression is very genuine. <br/> <br/>It''s interesting to compare yours to <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=53147" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">timfythetoo</a>''s ribbon winner. They are not disimilar, his is just more clearly overexposed across the frame. Your overexposure is spread equally across his face(flat lighting) whereas his shot shows a lighting ratio from side to side. This gives his girl''s face more depth.<br/> <br/>Sorry to compare yours to his but I think they are so similar that a comparison is helpful in picking out the reasons that his was well-received by the voters.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting! Mark</td>', 'Wow, surprised to see this one finished squarely on 5. I didn''t vote in the challenge but this one caught my eye. As some commentators mentioned, the inclusion of the blue sweatshirt probably hurt you in the score department. It would probably have been less of an issue if Riley''s eyes were blue. I love the tilt in his head and the expression is very genuine.  It''s interesting to compare yours to  timfythetoo''s ribbon winner. They are not disimilar, his is just more clearly overexposed across the frame. Your overexposure is spread equally across his face(flat lighting) whereas his shot shows a lighting ratio from side to side. This gives his girl''s face more depth. Sorry to compare yours to his but I think they are so similar that a comparison is helpful in picking out the reasons that his was well-received by the voters. Keep shooting! Mark', '2008-09-15 16:47:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956708, 716472, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>First of all, cute subject! <br/> <br/>I like the fact that you used 2 flashes, that means you''re trying to make more out of it than a snapshot. <br/> <br/>The light is pretty uneven. The shadows and highlights, close together, are almost like pure black and pure white. The fact that you used a flash at the left makes that effect even stronger. You might want to try to use the flash at the other side (with this photo) so the extra light can fill in the shadows (for example behind the bottle and at the shirt) The build-in flash is one you might want to avoid. It''s harsh and gives harsh shadows.<br/> <br/>I hope this comment was helpful for you!</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  First of all, cute subject!  I like the fact that you used 2 flashes, that means you''re trying to make more out of it than a snapshot.  The light is pretty uneven. The shadows and highlights, close together, are almost like pure black and pure white. The fact that you used a flash at the left makes that effect even stronger. You might want to try to use the flash at the other side (with this photo) so the extra light can fill in the shadows (for example behind the bottle and at the shirt) The build-in flash is one you might want to avoid. It''s harsh and gives harsh shadows. I hope this comment was helpful for you!', '2008-09-15 16:49:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956737, 717669, 51793, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)  <br/> <br/>Not sure why you wanted this image critiqued but okay here goes..<br/> <br/>It''s a good image but it slightly lacks interest. It does how ever give that thought to people of is he walking into the light? Is he being abducted? what exactly is going on ya know. I have to say that a 6.6 is pretty good.<br/> <br/>congrats on your top 10<br/> <br/>~Joe~</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :)   Not sure why you wanted this image critiqued but okay here goes.. It''s a good image but it slightly lacks interest. It does how ever give that thought to people of is he walking into the light? Is he being abducted? what exactly is going on ya know. I have to say that a 6.6 is pretty good. congrats on your top 10 ~Joe~', '2008-09-15 17:09:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956741, 717650, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>Yes, this is overexposed. But looking at your portfolio I think you can do better ;)<br/> <br/>The overexposed part almost has no detail left, while you could''ve done that and still remaining details. Also the half overexposed - half done right might be a bit too obvious, play with the lights and find out how you can do it in a different way.<br/> <br/>The colors of your eyes are great though, they really pop out of the photo. Are they as blue like this in real life too? ;)<br/> <br/>Hope this was a little helpful :)</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  Yes, this is overexposed. But looking at your portfolio I think you can do better ;) The overexposed part almost has no detail left, while you could''ve done that and still remaining details. Also the half overexposed - half done right might be a bit too obvious, play with the lights and find out how you can do it in a different way. The colors of your eyes are great though, they really pop out of the photo. Are they as blue like this in real life too? ;) Hope this was a little helpful :)', '2008-09-15 17:12:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956749, 717433, 51793, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :) <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>   The image lacks the overexposure that this challenge really calls for. Other than that the pet portrait isn''t really that interesting IMO. The image lacks what it needs to really catch the viewers eye. <br/> <br/>The fix:<br/>   I''m amazed that took 19th but most of the time it depends on what else is in the challenge. Take some time to think about what you want to shoot before you actually do. I read that this is a last minute submission and sometimes that works and sometimes it doesn''t. If you would have brought some more highlights into the image I think you could have scored better.<br/> <br/>~Joe~<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :)  First Impressions:    The image lacks the overexposure that this challenge really calls for. Other than that the pet portrait isn''t really that interesting IMO. The image lacks what it needs to really catch the viewers eye.  The fix:   I''m amazed that took 19th but most of the time it depends on what else is in the challenge. Take some time to think about what you want to shoot before you actually do. I read that this is a last minute submission and sometimes that works and sometimes it doesn''t. If you would have brought some more highlights into the image I think you could have scored better. ~Joe~ ', '2008-09-15 17:16:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956758, 715109, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>The expression of your buddy is pretty cute, but my experience learned that expressions like these don''t really work here in challenges; this way it looks more like a snapshot.<br/> <br/>The thing with challenges is also that you need to see the technique or subject in the entry what the challenge is about. I don''t see "overexposed" in your photo, only the background, and that might just be in a studio. <br/> <br/>Good luck in photography, I see in your other entries you have a good eye for good moments!!</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  The expression of your buddy is pretty cute, but my experience learned that expressions like these don''t really work here in challenges; this way it looks more like a snapshot. The thing with challenges is also that you need to see the technique or subject in the entry what the challenge is about. I don''t see "overexposed" in your photo, only the background, and that might just be in a studio.  Good luck in photography, I see in your other entries you have a good eye for good moments!!', '2008-09-15 17:26:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956841, 717167, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique club. First le tme say I think this deserved a better score then it received. This is easily a high five low 6 photo, even by DPC''s standards. I love the clarity, the colors, meeting the challenge, creative use of timed exposure to get what you needed. One thing I will bring to the table, is I always recommend at least one and usually two borders on entries here, the presentation is just so much more appealing to voters. I highly recommend it. Otherwise I''m not sure what the voters were looking for here, its def exposed to the right with blown highlights. Voters......go figure.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique club. First le tme say I think this deserved a better score then it received. This is easily a high five low 6 photo, even by DPC''s standards. I love the clarity, the colors, meeting the challenge, creative use of timed exposure to get what you needed. One thing I will bring to the table, is I always recommend at least one and usually two borders on entries here, the presentation is just so much more appealing to voters. I highly recommend it. Otherwise I''m not sure what the voters were looking for here, its def exposed to the right with blown highlights. Voters......go figure.', '2008-09-15 18:12:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956893, 716608, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club. <br/> <br/>First you did meet the challenge, def overexposed, now the question is, does it enhance your photo? That I''m not so sure it does. The overexposure is actually distracting and doesnt enhance the photo. I think the subject is a bit crowded as it is and a bit busy. I''m not sure but it might also be a bit oversharpened. <br/> <br/>Now how to make this a better entry? Honestly I have sat and thought about how I could make this subject more interesting and over exposed at the same time, and I cant honestly come up with an idea. Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club.  First you did meet the challenge, def overexposed, now the question is, does it enhance your photo? That I''m not so sure it does. The overexposure is actually distracting and doesnt enhance the photo. I think the subject is a bit crowded as it is and a bit busy. I''m not sure but it might also be a bit oversharpened.  Now how to make this a better entry? Honestly I have sat and thought about how I could make this subject more interesting and over exposed at the same time, and I cant honestly come up with an idea. Good luck in future challenges.', '2008-09-15 18:29:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956982, 717461, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review<br/> <br/>This image meets the challenge, as it is defiently over exposed.  However, the large bright area on the right side of the image is very distracting, and seems not to serve a purpose.  I see you raised the ISO, and used a longer shutter opening to get the over exposure.  I think the higher ISO gave you the noise and grain that appear here.  More light, with a lower ISO and shorter exposure could help here.<br/> <br/>Had the mask been a little darker, it would have stood out more.  If you look at some of the higly ranked entries you can see what I mean.  <br/> <br/>I do like the mask, and the expression on the mask.  I think you have something to work with here.</td>', 'Critique Club Review This image meets the challenge, as it is defiently over exposed.  However, the large bright area on the right side of the image is very distracting, and seems not to serve a purpose.  I see you raised the ISO, and used a longer shutter opening to get the over exposure.  I think the higher ISO gave you the noise and grain that appear here.  More light, with a lower ISO and shorter exposure could help here. Had the mask been a little darker, it would have stood out more.  If you look at some of the higly ranked entries you can see what I mean.   I do like the mask, and the expression on the mask.  I think you have something to work with here.', '2008-09-15 19:00:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957024, 717248, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review<br/> <br/>I can''t quite decide if this is nice and sharp, or a bit soft.  Perhaps depth of field is just a little shallow.  The center of the flower is sharp, but the edges of the petals are a little soft.  <br/> <br/>Lighting is flat, and the subject is centered, which also probably cost you a few votes.  Some angle to the flower, as opposed to head on, would be beneficial also.<br/> <br/>I do like the colors, and the way it fades to white at the edges on the left of the flower.  This to me, is the strongest part of the image.  If you could carry that through the image, it should do better in the voting.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Review I can''t quite decide if this is nice and sharp, or a bit soft.  Perhaps depth of field is just a little shallow.  The center of the flower is sharp, but the edges of the petals are a little soft.   Lighting is flat, and the subject is centered, which also probably cost you a few votes.  Some angle to the flower, as opposed to head on, would be beneficial also. I do like the colors, and the way it fades to white at the edges on the left of the flower.  This to me, is the strongest part of the image.  If you could carry that through the image, it should do better in the voting. ', '2008-09-15 19:20:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957041, 716841, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a> PostLuminous Award Nominee<br/>So simple, and yet so much style, so dynamic</td>', ' PostLuminous Award NomineeSo simple, and yet so much style, so dynamic', '2008-09-15 19:26:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957042, 717216, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a> PostLuminous Award Nominee<br/>This image is compelling and captivating... very well done</td>', ' PostLuminous Award NomineeThis image is compelling and captivating... very well done', '2008-09-15 19:26:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957043, 717536, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a> PostLuminous Award Nominee<br/>so very well done, an image to be proud of</td>', ' PostLuminous Award Nomineeso very well done, an image to be proud of', '2008-09-15 19:27:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957047, 717592, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a> PostLuminous Award Nominee<br/>An extraordinary interplay of lines, forms, light, shadows, shades.  Well seen, well composed, well done!</td>', ' PostLuminous Award NomineeAn extraordinary interplay of lines, forms, light, shadows, shades.  Well seen, well composed, well done!', '2008-09-15 19:28:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957062, 717264, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677020" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg"/></a> PostLuminous Award Winner<br/>Lovely subject, daring approach, creative.  Leaves the impression that one is seeing more than is actually there. Very engaging image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-16 05:24:55.</i></td>', ' PostLuminous Award WinnerLovely subject, daring approach, creative.  Leaves the impression that one is seeing more than is actually there. Very engaging image.', '2008-09-15 19:35:06.000000', '2008-09-16 06:24:55.000000', 0),
(4957096, 717711, 7743, '<td valign="top">*** Greetings from the Critique Club ***<br/> <br/>First impressions: The high key works here.<br/> <br/>Exposure: You did well to keep a good balance between lights and darks though I feel the left side of the face is a little too light or the other side a little too dark giving the eyes a bit of a spooky look rather than natural.<br/> <br/>Impact:  High key effect I think gives this image its impact making the subject really stand out.<br/> <br/>Composition: I thinking this may work better with a more vertical composition, hence cropping more on the right and left.  One hand appears to be cut off at the wrist though not really a problem since it''s behind the boy and at the point of blending into the background.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting.<br/> <br/>Cheers!<br/> <br/>Colette</td>', '*** Greetings from the Critique Club *** First impressions: The high key works here. Exposure: You did well to keep a good balance between lights and darks though I feel the left side of the face is a little too light or the other side a little too dark giving the eyes a bit of a spooky look rather than natural. Impact:  High key effect I think gives this image its impact making the subject really stand out. Composition: I thinking this may work better with a more vertical composition, hence cropping more on the right and left.  One hand appears to be cut off at the wrist though not really a problem since it''s behind the boy and at the point of blending into the background. Keep shooting. Cheers! Colette', '2008-09-15 20:04:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957244, 715233, 23098, '<td valign="top">Good take on the challenge and nicely overexposed. This is good in more ways than one.</td>', 'Good take on the challenge and nicely overexposed. This is good in more ways than one.', '2008-09-15 21:49:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957370, 717568, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast:  Image is mildly over exposed, which is part of the challenge.  I think perhaps it could be taken up a bit more with an increase in the contrast.  I''d like to see the rocks a little lighter, a little brighter, but would still want the figure dark the way it is now.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Focus is nice and sharp.  Depth of field is great.<br/> <br/>There is really not much more you can do with this image.  What makes the image is all the detail in the rocks, and the sky.  If you brightened all that much more, the detail would be lost, and the final result would be less than you have now.<br/> <br/>I see what looks like a small island beyond the subject.  Perhaps that against a bright sea and bright sky, would have worked better for an overexposed challenge.<br/> <br/>This is an excellent image, just one that has a harder time carrying the theme of the challenge.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Brightness and Contrast:  Image is mildly over exposed, which is part of the challenge.  I think perhaps it could be taken up a bit more with an increase in the contrast.  I''d like to see the rocks a little lighter, a little brighter, but would still want the figure dark the way it is now. Focus and depth of field:  Focus is nice and sharp.  Depth of field is great. There is really not much more you can do with this image.  What makes the image is all the detail in the rocks, and the sky.  If you brightened all that much more, the detail would be lost, and the final result would be less than you have now. I see what looks like a small island beyond the subject.  Perhaps that against a bright sea and bright sky, would have worked better for an overexposed challenge. This is an excellent image, just one that has a harder time carrying the theme of the challenge.', '2008-09-15 23:47:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957571, 716841, 68586, '<td valign="top">Great shot - love the pose and PP work.<br/> <br/>Manages to convey movement even though the guy is standing still.</td>', 'Great shot - love the pose and PP work. Manages to convey movement even though the guy is standing still.', '2008-09-16 03:38:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957994, 715270, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This shot instantly reminded me of the Haunted Mansion at Disneyland. I think you chose great subject to overexpose. <br/> <br/>I like the angle you used for this shot. It gives the house a grandiose presence, and captures the plant growth that has invaded. I particularly like the plants that seem to be bursting through the ceiling on the porch. The delicate branch reaching towards the house on the left is great too. It brings some good detail and life to the mess of foliage. <br/> <br/>A couple of my favorite elements of this shot are the lines along the top of the roof, and around the roof trim. The subtle line outlining the very top is excellent. Without this, I may have thought it was too overexposed. The shadows and contrast in the trim also bring some nice detail to the shot  and a perfect place too, since my eyes are drawn to that corner.<br/> <br/>I wasnt so sure about the hanging leaves on the upper left at first. I thought they seemed too out of focus, and looked almost like a painting. However, the more I look at the shot, the more I like them. They really add to the mood. The plants at the bottom are also well lit, without being overexposed. You left the overexposed-ness to the main subject of the shot, the house. Well done. <br/> <br/>I also think you made the right choice by going black &amp; white. My only suggestion for improvement may have been to bring a tad more detail out of the right column. Its not really necessary though. And Im not sure howd you manage it.<br/> <br/>Overall, a great shot. The more I look at it, the more I like it. IMO, your score should have been closer to the 7-8 range.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This shot instantly reminded me of the Haunted Mansion at Disneyland. I think you chose great subject to overexpose.  I like the angle you used for this shot. It gives the house a grandiose presence, and captures the plant growth that has invaded. I particularly like the plants that seem to be bursting through the ceiling on the porch. The delicate branch reaching towards the house on the left is great too. It brings some good detail and life to the mess of foliage.  A couple of my favorite elements of this shot are the lines along the top of the roof, and around the roof trim. The subtle line outlining the very top is excellent. Without this, I may have thought it was too overexposed. The shadows and contrast in the trim also bring some nice detail to the shot  and a perfect place too, since my eyes are drawn to that corner. I wasnt so sure about the hanging leaves on the upper left at first. I thought they seemed too out of focus, and looked almost like a painting. However, the more I look at the shot, the more I like them. They really add to the mood. The plants at the bottom are also well lit, without being overexposed. You left the overexposed-ness to the main subject of the shot, the house. Well done.  I also think you made the right choice by going black & white. My only suggestion for improvement may have been to bring a tad more detail out of the right column. Its not really necessary though. And Im not sure howd you manage it. Overall, a great shot. The more I look at it, the more I like it. IMO, your score should have been closer to the 7-8 range.', '2008-09-16 12:58:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4958226, 717291, 98041, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a great capture.<br/>And congrats on 5th place XD!</td>', 'I thought this was a great capture.And congrats on 5th place XD!', '2008-09-16 14:46:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4958410, 717609, 56275, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>Well first of all, this is an absolutely adorable shot. The expression on her face is priceless. <br/> <br/>Colors: I agree with the comment about the overexposure brining out her eyes. Wonder if bumping up the blue saturation would make them stand out a little more? I love the red dress. Works well with the greens in the background, and stands out from her pale skin. <br/> <br/>Lighting: Some comments say you didnt overexpose enough. I disagree. I think if you went too much more, youd lose the detail in her expression, and possibly lose sight of her hair. <br/> <br/>Framing: Good job framing / cropping as well. Good use of the rule of thirds. <br/> <br/>Critiques: One of the first things I noticed was the lines on her head. Almost looked like a painting on canvas. Its not a deal breaker, but it is a little distracting. Also, I think Id prefer it without the thread / grass on her dress. I realize this was more of an impromptu shot, so its not a big deal. <br/> <br/>Overall, you captured a great moment, and it met the challenge well. I think voters may have skipped by this photo too quickly to enjoy all of the subtleties of the shot.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Well first of all, this is an absolutely adorable shot. The expression on her face is priceless.  Colors: I agree with the comment about the overexposure brining out her eyes. Wonder if bumping up the blue saturation would make them stand out a little more? I love the red dress. Works well with the greens in the background, and stands out from her pale skin.  Lighting: Some comments say you didnt overexpose enough. I disagree. I think if you went too much more, youd lose the detail in her expression, and possibly lose sight of her hair.  Framing: Good job framing / cropping as well. Good use of the rule of thirds.  Critiques: One of the first things I noticed was the lines on her head. Almost looked like a painting on canvas. Its not a deal breaker, but it is a little distracting. Also, I think Id prefer it without the thread / grass on her dress. I realize this was more of an impromptu shot, so its not a big deal.  Overall, you captured a great moment, and it met the challenge well. I think voters may have skipped by this photo too quickly to enjoy all of the subtleties of the shot.', '2008-09-16 17:05:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959375, 717711, 30982, '<td valign="top">Hmmm.  I''m thinking I may prefer this with the grain over the Neat Image.  Though I use it, I''m not a huge fan of that tool.  I do like the chocolate tones.  He''s got a little too much of a sweetness to his expression to make it creepy or weirded out, to my eye.  So no, no chocolate for you!  Well, OK, maybe some later... if you''re good.</td>', 'Hmmm.  I''m thinking I may prefer this with the grain over the Neat Image.  Though I use it, I''m not a huge fan of that tool.  I do like the chocolate tones.  He''s got a little too much of a sweetness to his expression to make it creepy or weirded out, to my eye.  So no, no chocolate for you!  Well, OK, maybe some later... if you''re good.', '2008-09-17 07:44:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959382, 717741, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very strong composition and the high key/overexposure on the eyes works quite nicely here.  Makes a nice companion piece - a bit more edgy - to your other SP.</td>', 'Very strong composition and the high key/overexposure on the eyes works quite nicely here.  Makes a nice companion piece - a bit more edgy - to your other SP.', '2008-09-17 07:47:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959383, 716703, 30982, '<td valign="top">Oh, this is lovely!  Wonderful use of overexposure to create a minimalistic and compelling landscape.  Very nice!</td>', 'Oh, this is lovely!  Wonderful use of overexposure to create a minimalistic and compelling landscape.  Very nice!', '2008-09-17 07:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959384, 717331, 30982, '<td valign="top">I love how the bear seems almost poured out of the lightness at the top of the frame!</td>', 'I love how the bear seems almost poured out of the lightness at the top of the frame!', '2008-09-17 07:50:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959685, 717568, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ambaker:</b></div><hr/><i> Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast:  Image is mildly over exposed, which is part of the challenge.  I think perhaps it could be taken up a bit more with an increase in the contrast.  I''d like to see the rocks a little lighter, a little brighter, but would still want the figure dark the way it is now.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Focus is nice and sharp.  Depth of field is great.<br/> <br/>There is really not much more you can do with this image.  What makes the image is all the detail in the rocks, and the sky.  If you brightened all that much more, the detail would be lost, and the final result would be less than you have now.<br/> <br/>I see what looks like a small island beyond the subject.  Perhaps that against a bright sea and bright sky, would have worked better for an overexposed challenge.<br/> <br/>This is an excellent image, just one that has a harder time carrying the theme of the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Many thanks Alex for your good critique - much appreciated.</td>', 'Originally posted by ambaker: Critique Club Review: Brightness and Contrast:  Image is mildly over exposed, which is part of the challenge.  I think perhaps it could be taken up a bit more with an increase in the contrast.  I''d like to see the rocks a little lighter, a little brighter, but would still want the figure dark the way it is now. Focus and depth of field:  Focus is nice and sharp.  Depth of field is great. There is really not much more you can do with this image.  What makes the image is all the detail in the rocks, and the sky.  If you brightened all that much more, the detail would be lost, and the final result would be less than you have now. I see what looks like a small island beyond the subject.  Perhaps that against a bright sea and bright sky, would have worked better for an overexposed challenge. This is an excellent image, just one that has a harder time carrying the theme of the challenge.   Many thanks Alex for your good critique - much appreciated.', '2008-09-17 11:32:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959756, 715273, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very pretty.  I love the starbursts - they give the scene a magical quality.  The one at the bottom adds particular beauty to that area where the light is highlighting the tops of the weed things (are those cattails? no clue) <br/> <br/>Btw - I save sharpening for last.  I do all the editing, resize and then apply it.</td>', 'Very pretty.  I love the starbursts - they give the scene a magical quality.  The one at the bottom adds particular beauty to that area where the light is highlighting the tops of the weed things (are those cattails? no clue)  Btw - I save sharpening for last.  I do all the editing, resize and then apply it.', '2008-09-17 12:01:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4960148, 717214, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like this!!  I love how the pelican appears only after you view for a second or two.  And I like how either the pelican is claiming the spot, or the big rock is.  I really do think the overexposure worked very well here.  Nicely balanced, very crisp and clean.  And I just read your other comments - Tim is a hard guy to please and he liked this one, too.</td>', 'I like this!!  I love how the pelican appears only after you view for a second or two.  And I like how either the pelican is claiming the spot, or the big rock is.  I really do think the overexposure worked very well here.  Nicely balanced, very crisp and clean.  And I just read your other comments - Tim is a hard guy to please and he liked this one, too.', '2008-09-17 15:00:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4961355, 715429, 61961, '<td valign="top">This was DQ''d?  So sorry.  It was (is) a beautiful image.  Hope you aren''t too discouraged.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'This was DQ''d?  So sorry.  It was (is) a beautiful image.  Hope you aren''t too discouraged.  Keep up the good work.', '2008-09-18 09:36:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4963292, 715223, 96751, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your wonderful comments.  I''ve been out of town and just got back.  I''m thrilled to have placed this high in the challenge.  Learning something every day.  Including how to interpret the challenges :-)</td>', 'Thank you all for your wonderful comments.  I''ve been out of town and just got back.  I''m thrilled to have placed this high in the challenge.  Learning something every day.  Including how to interpret the challenges :-)', '2008-09-19 02:11:16.000000', NULL, 0),
